    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0334" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150.071 Control/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Netherlands Legation to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1280</seg></opener>
                <p>The Royal Netherland Legation presents its compliments to the Department of State
                    and has the honor to enclose herewith copy of its <hi rendition="#italic">Note
                        Verbale</hi> of January 17, 1928, No. 170,<anchor n="67" xml:id="d238-f1"/>
                    with the request <pb facs="0335" n="255" xml:id="pg255"/> that the State
                    Department will kindly consider the contents of said note applicable to the bill
                    (S. 202) providing for the deportation of certain alien seamen, which was
                    ordered reported favorably from the Committee on Immigration of the Senate on
                    April 7th, 1930.<anchor n="68" xml:id="d238-f2"/></p>
                <p>The Royal Legation presents its anticipated thanks to the Department of State for
                    what might be done in this respect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1930-04-08">April 8,
                            1930</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
